	"schema_version": 1,
	"purpose": "Crew-reported slip positions at the public ferry landings: where a boat sits when it is landed in each slip. An input to the landing survey; not a hydrographic survey, a chart correction or a navigation aid.",
	"source": "crew-reported: project crew reviewer, slip positions 2026-11",
	"received": "2026-11-10",
	"point_meaning": "Each position is the boat's own GPS position while landed in that slip, as [latitude, longitude] in WGS84 degrees. The point is on the boat, not on the barge: the barge face is ahead of it by the distance from the GPS antenna to the bow, along the boat's landed heading. Neither that distance nor the heading is given.",
	"limitations": "Which boats and receivers produced the fixes, where the antenna sits on each boat, and whether a position is a single fix or an average are not known. Treat each point as good to a few metres at best. Slip names are the crew's. Operator facilities that are not public landings are not included.",
